anything which can be named (अभिधेय), a category or predicament;
 the number of such categories, according to the Vaiśeṣikas, is seven;
 according to the Sāṅkhyas, twenty-five (or twenty-seven according to
 the followers of Patañjali), and two according to the Vedāntins.

